{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"RCA (investigation only; no code change yet). Root cause CONFIRMED — hypothesis 1, in a specific form: process retirement, not client disconnect.\n\nEvidence (tickets branch + host autodeploy journal, times PDT 2026-10-27):\n- 22:11:31 EDIT (boxes ticked). 22:12:06 autodeploy cut /mcp over to the new 339c0b3 backend; 22:12:07 `docker stop --time 1260` (SIGTERM) sent to the old backend rebar-mcp-58991ec55876-8092 while the close was in flight on it.\n- 22:14:01 COMPLETION_VERDICT PASS written by the close (verified_at_sha 339c0b3; plan material recomputes to 61a3ad8cb11e3d44, identical to the later signature) -> verifier DID run (hyp. 2 refuted).\n- 22:14:08 STATUS in_progress->closed, completion_expectation=required. No SIGNATURE. Old container observed exited at 22:14:12. No other store writes 22:10:51-22:27:21 (hyp. 3 refuted).\n\nMechanism on main (f13aaa04c2d):\n1. `_mcp_health.CERTIFIED_TOOLS` = review_plan/verify_completion/review_code/scan_spec. `transition_ticket` is not gauge-tracked, so the SIGTERM drain saw 0 in flight and set should_exit at once; uvicorn's 30 s backstop then dropped the request (\"Transport closed\").\n2. The tool body runs on an AnyIO worker with abandon_on_cancel=True; that non-daemon thread keeps running and keeps the process alive.\n3. `run_mcp` returns, and `mcp_server.main()`'s `finally: binding.cleanup()` deletes the box signer's key copy.\n4. verify.completion_pinned_ticket_view is off, so the close takes the legacy path: STATUS commits, then `_sign_completion_and_report` hits SigningError \"the bound op-cert key ... does not exist\", degrades to cause=sign_failed (stderr only), the thread ends, the process exits.\n\nReproduction (local, no LLM, 0 live gate runs): scratch probe binds a compose_signer box key, runs `_sign_completion_and_report` on a copied-context worker after `binding.cleanup()` -> `{'signed': False, 'cause': 'sign_failed', ...key ... does not exist}`, 0 SIGNATURE files; control without cleanup -> signed, 1 SIGNATURE.\n\nA pure client disconnect does NOT cause this: the abandoned worker still finishes and the key still exists. A second instance matches the same pattern: trifling-countable-armadillo (859c-760d) closed 2026-09-20 04:03:20 PDT, 2 min after a retire SIGTERM at 04:01:20, completion_expectation=required, no completion-verifier attestation.\n\nStore survey (origin/tickets): 934 closed with completion_expectation=required; 931 carry a completion-verifier attestation; 3 do not and carry no FORCE_CLOSE: damageable-huge-xiphosuran, cutprice-untameable-stork, trifling-countable-armadillo. Forced closes are already distinguishable in data: their STATUS records completion_expectation=force_bypassed (72 closes).\n\nClaim-gate audit (AC4): claim_ticket mints no certificate (it verifies an existing plan-review attestation); review_plan, which signs, is gauge-tracked. The same key-cleanup race applies to any signing tool body still running after run_mcp returns.\n\nPrior intent: story b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618 built the atomic close bundle behind verify.completion_pinned_ticket_view and recorded \"Default enablement is separate and evidence-based\". The legacy sign_failed degrade (story 8d8e; silvern-dewy-damselfly) is deliberate. Fix direction needs an operator decision; paused before review-plan/claim."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793506128627247001,"uuid":"3989e326-a747-432f-854d-bdcbc11e3ea3"}